// THE DATED SUCCESSOR, AND THE FIRST RECEIPT THAT CAN NAME THE SEAM ITS PEAK WAS ESTABLISHED IN
// (this change's own CI run 35652545009, job 106508550698, srv3-01, 2026-09-21, twenty-three beats
// at sixty seconds, every beat derived from its own `[floor-cgroup] seam= stall_per_min=` line by
// the instrument rather than joined to a neighbouring line by a reader). It supersedes
// gunbc_floor_memory_stat_receipt_2026_09_19 as gunbc_floor_held_set_standing's input; that
// receipt is RETAINED, not deleted, because it is the evidence the 26/25 GiB row was argued from
// and a superseded reading is history rather than a mistake.
//
// WHAT IT SHOWS, AND IT IS NOT WHAT A PEAK SNAPSHOT WOULD HAVE SAID -- the SHAPE of the rows
// below, which is the part a reader cannot get by looking up one number. receipt_peak_seam names
// the peak's seam: it is in the claim-evaluation fold. But the held set rises MONOTONICALLY across
// every preparation beat and never falls, so almost all of the peak is built before the fold
// begins and is still held while the fold runs; the fold adds a comparatively small working set on
// top. The peak SEAM and the demand's CAUSE are therefore different answers, and a reduction aimed
// at the seam where the maximum occurs would chase the smaller term. The retained preparation set
// is the subject.
//
// IT IS NOT A CACHE STORY AND THE ROWS SAY SO DIRECTLY rather than by inference: the file counter
// is FLAT across every preparation beat and then FALLS during the fold. That is reclaim giving the
// cache back to make room for anonymous memory, which is the opposite of cache accumulation -- a
// direction, readable off the rows, that no single beat could establish.
//
// PROCESS OVERLAP IS NOT RULED OUT BY THESE ROWS AND MUST NOT BE SAID TO BE. The anonymous set
// falling after the peak is CONSISTENT with the fold releasing retained state, but consistency is
// not discrimination: these counters are per-cgroup totals and say nothing about which processes
// held what, so no reading here separates one process growing from two overlapping. Overlap is
// recorded as UNOBSERVED in floor_receipt_uncarried_observation_frontier, and its line there names
// a missing INSTRUMENT rather than a missing transcription. The cache arm is excluded by the rows;
// the overlap arm is simply not measured, and those are different states.
//
// SWITCHING THE STANDING MOVES TWO DERIVED QUANTITIES, NOT ONE, and the second is easy to miss
// because nothing reds when it changes. The demand is the obvious one: floor_memory_requirement
// reads this receipt's peak. The other is the GUEST CACHE ALLOWANCE -- gunbc.runner_microvm
// gunbc_runner_microvm_guest_cache_allowance derives it from receipt_last_unstalled_beat, which
// selects a different beat on this receipt than on its predecessor, so the allowance moves with
// the standing and in the opposite direction to the demand.
//
// THE PRODUCERS ARE NAMED AND THE FIGURES ARE NOT COPIED HERE (DESIGN 6; review 69874). An earlier
// revision of this note carried both moves as byte counts, which is the same defect this change
// REMOVES from gunbc.runner_microvm's allowance note one file over -- deleting a transcribed beat
// figure there and minting transcribed figures here would have moved the rot rather than ending
// it, and the next standing switch would falsify these sentences exactly as it falsified that one.
// Each quantity lives in its one home: the demand in this receipt's rows through
// floor_memory_requirement, the allowance in gunbc_runner_microvm_guest_cache_allowance, the
// remainder comparison in the shape-fit fold and its expecting-red probe.
//
// WHY THE CONSEQUENCE IS STATED AT ALL, given the figures are not: every claim over these
// quantities is derivation-relative and stays green through the change -- including the production
// shape's expecting-red probe, which still refuses, by a narrower margin than before. A quantity
// that moves a fleet's sizing without reddening anything is exactly the change that lands
// unnoticed, so the FACT that it moves is named at the row that moves it, and a reader who wants
// the margin evaluates the fold.
//
// ITS WORKLOAD RAN TO ITS END, WHICH IS WHY run_completed IS TRUE ON A RUN THAT REFUSED. The
// floor executed preparation and the whole claim-evaluation fold -- twenty-three beats, the
// anonymous set rising to its peak and falling again as the fold released scopes -- and the
// refusal came afterwards, from an unrelated lane (a local-repo wet terminal in
// test.claim.mtcollins1_census_image_local_wet, a module this change does not touch). The peak is
// therefore not truncated, which is the only question that field's consumer asks.
//
// STILL CENSORED, AND THE POLICY IS WHY. This ran at the live 26/25 GiB row with swap available,
// and its own rows record the consequence: the peak beat's stall is NON-ZERO and the stalls rise
// steeply across the beats after it, while the run's heartbeat shows host swap-in climbing. So
// this receipt's peak is a LOWER BOUND on what the run wanted to hold, for the same reason the
// 2026-09-19 figure was -- and receipt_peak_reading_standing DERIVES exactly that, answering
// PeakIsLowerBound with the stalling peak beat as its cause rather than leaving a reader to
// compare stall figures by eye. A cell whose MemoryHigh sits under the workload cannot
// produce an uncensored demand reading by construction; only a run with no throttle line and no
// swap can, which is the shape gunbc.runner_slot_allocation's shakedown slot declares and which
// nothing can dispatch yet.
data gunbc_floor_memory_stat_receipt_2026_09_21: FloorHeldSetReceipt = FloorHeldSetReceipt {
